<details><summary>Solution</summary>$$ \sqrt{n-1}<\frac12(\sqrt n+\sqrt{n-1})<\sqrt n $$    $$ \frac1{\sqrt n}<\frac2{\sqrt n+\sqrt{n-1}}<\frac1{\sqrt{n-1}} $$    $$ \frac1{\sqrt n}<2(\sqrt n-\sqrt{n-1})<\frac1{\sqrt{n-1}} $$  This shows that
\begin{align*}
1+\frac1{\sqrt2}+\frac1{\sqrt3}+\cdots+\frac1{\sqrt{99}}&>2(\sqrt2-\sqrt1)+2(\sqrt3-\sqrt2)+2(\sqrt4-\sqrt3)+\cdots+2(\sqrt{100}-\sqrt{99})
&=2(-\sqrt1)+2(\sqrt{100})
&=18
\end{align*}
This implies that  $S-\frac1{\sqrt{100}}>18\implies S>18.01$ \begin{align*}
