Is the area of triangle  $BCP$  really still determined if  $ABCD$  isn't specified as a *convex* quadrilateral? I'm having trouble figuring that out. Assuming  $ABCD$  is convex, here is my solution.

[asy]
pair A,C,D,B,P;
A=(3,5);
C=(9,0);
D=(0,0);
B=rotate(62.5,A)*C;
P=rotate(62.5,A)*D;
draw(A--C--D--cycle);
add(rotate(62.5,A)*currentpicture);
draw(B--C);
path r=B--P;
