We begin by using the following well-known lemma:

<span style="color:red">**Lemma:**</span> If  $a+b$  is an integer but  $a$  and  $b$  are not integers,  $\lfloor a \rfloor + \lfloor b \rfloor = a + b - 1$ .

This can be proven by expressing  $\lfloor x \rfloor = x - \{x\}$ .  ${\color{red} \blacksquare}$ <span style="color:blue">**Claim:**</span> For an odd prime  $p$ ,  $\left\lfloor\dfrac{x^p}{p}\right\rfloor + \left\lfloor\dfrac{(p-x)^p}{p}\right\rfloor \equiv -1 \mod p$ .

\begin{align*}
\left\lfloor\dfrac{x^p}{p}\right\rfloor + \left\lfloor\dfrac{(p-x)^p}{p}\right\rfloor &\equiv \frac{x^p + (p-x)^p}{p} - 1 
&\equiv \frac{- (p) \cdot (p) \cdot (x^{p-1})}{p} - 1 
&\equiv -1 \mod p.~{\color{blue} \blacksquare}
\end{align*}

Thus we can seperate our sum into 1007 pairs for  $x = 2,~\ldots~, 1008$ , plus  $\left\lfloor\dfrac{1^p}{p}\right\rfloor = 0$ , so our answer is  $-1007 \implies \boxed{1010}$ .  $\blacksquare$

