We have
\begin{eqnarray*}
\sum _{i=1}^{2015}\left\lfloor\frac{i^{2017}}{2017}\right\rfloor&\equiv &\sum _{i=1}^{2016}\frac{i^{2017}-i}{2017}-\left\lfloor\frac{2016^{2017}}{2017}\right\rfloor\pmod{2017}
&\equiv& \frac{\sum _{i=2}^{2017}}{2017}(i-1)^{2017}-\sum _{i=1}^{2016}\frac{i}{2017}-\left\lfloor\frac{2016^{2017}}{2017}\right\rfloor\pmod{2017}
&\equiv& 0-1008-2016\equiv 1010\pmod{2017}
\end{eqnarray*}
where the first line follows FLT and second line follows LTE ( $2016^{2017}+1^{2017}\equiv 0$ (mod  $p^2$ ) and  $2016^{2017}\equiv -1$  (mod  $p^2$ ) and  $\left\lfloor\frac{2016^{2017}}{2017}\right\rfloor \equiv 2016$  (mod  $p$ )).

Note that by Fermat's Little Theorem, we have  $k^p\equiv k\pmod p$ , so  $\left\lfloor \frac{k^p}{p}\right\rfloor = \frac{k^p-k}{p}$ . We wish to compute: \begin{align*}\frac{(1^p+2^p+\cdots+2015^p)-(1+2+\cdots+2015)}{p}\pmod p. \end{align*} Note that   $$ k^p + (2017-k)^p\equiv 0\pmod {p^2}. $$   Thus, pairing up every  $k^p$  with  $(2017-k)^p$ , we see that  $1^p+2^p+\cdots+2015^p\equiv 1\pmod {p^2}$ . Therefore,  $(1^p+2^p+\cdots+2015^p)-(1+2+\cdots+2015)\equiv 2017^2 -1008(2015) + 1\pmod {p^2}$ . Finally, we have: \begin{align*}&\frac{(1^p+2^p+\cdots+2015^p)-(1+2+\cdots+2015)}{2017}
&\equiv \frac{2017^2 -1008(2015) + 1}{2017}
&\equiv \boxed{1010}\pmod {p}\end{align*}

