Let  $M_A$ ,  $M_B$ ,  $M_C$  be the arc midpoints of  $\widehat{BC}$ ,  $\widehat{AB}$  and  $\widehat{AC}$ . We claim  $M_A$  is the fixed point. By Incenter-Excenter Lemma we know that,
\begin{align*}
M_BI_B = M_BA = M_CA = M_CI_C
\end{align*}
and paired with the fact that  $M_AM_B = M_AM_C$  we know that  $\triangle M_AM_BI_B \sim M_AM_CI_C$  with ratio  $1$ . This forces  $M_AI_B = M_AI_C$ . Now this means  $M_A$  is the Miquel point of  $I_BM_BM_CI_C$  and hence  $M_A \in (I_BI_CP)$  and so we're done.

The statement is equivalent to
\[[APO]+[AOQ]=[APQ].\]
WLOG assume  $\overline{AO}=1,$  so  $\sqrt{2}=\overline{AH}=2\times\sin{\angle B}\times\sin{\angle C}\quad(\star)$  by the given condiction. Furthermore\[\overline{AP}=\sqrt{2}\sin{\angle B},\overline{PH}=\sqrt{2}\cos{\angle B},\overline{AQ}=\sqrt{2}\sin{\angle C},\overline{QH}=\sqrt{2}\cos{\angle C}.\]
Therefore it suffices to prove that
\[\begin{aligned}
\sqrt{2} \sin{\angle B} \cos{\angle C} + \sqrt{2} \sin{\angle C} \cos{\angle B} &= 2\sin{\angle B} \sin{\angle C} \sin{\angle A}&
\sqrt{2} \sin{\left(\angle B + \angle C\right)}&=2 \times \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} \sin{\angle A}&(\text{follows by ( $\star$ )})
\sin{\angle A} &= \sin{\angle A}.
\end{aligned}\]
So we are done.  $\square$ [asy]
